<title>LITHUANIA: BOURSE CAPITALISATION SLIDES.</title>
<headline>BOURSE CAPITALISATION SLIDES.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The capitalisation of the Vilnius</p>
<p>bourse slipped to 5.186 billion litas last week from 5.211</p>
<p>billion litas the previous week, the stock exchange said on</p>
<p>Tuesday.</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse statistics:</p>
<p>					    June 23-27     June 16-20</p>
<p>    Submitted orders		  16,985	   16,367</p>
<p>    Executed orders		   992		1,079</p>
<p>Number of transactions on</p>
<p>    Central market (CM)	     729		865</p>
<p>    Turnover on the CM in LTL     4,169,790	2,314,210</p>
<p>Number of transactions in</p>
<p>    block trades (BT)		 130		107</p>
<p>    Turnover of BT in LTL	   16,440,800     12,033,210</p>
<p>    Supply of shares per week     60,766,923     59,209,584</p>
<p>    Demand of shares per week     3,605,856	4,118,952</p>
<p>Turnover of shares</p>
<p>    on CM per week in LTL	   1,925,950	2,262,170</p>
<p>    in BT per week in LTL	   6,360,130	12,033,210</p>
<p>The number of transactions</p>
<p>    in government T-bills	   20		 4</p>
<p>The turnover of government</p>
<p>    T-bills in LTL per week	 12,324,510     52,035</p>
<p>-- Burton Frierson, Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 17</p>
